              "type": "PMID",
              "notes": "Highlights that GBM cells reside in a highly altered extracellular matrix environment rich in hyaluronan and collagens, which interact with tumor cell surface receptors like CD44 to influence proliferation and migration ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10046791/#:~:text=Hyaluronan%20is%20a%20linear%20and,growth%2C%20cellular%20proliferation%2C%20and%20cellular)) ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10046791/#:~:text=Normal%20brain%20tissue%20ECMs%20are,have%20shown%20that%20GBM%20cell))"
