        "Immune evasion via reduced antigen presentation and immunosuppressive signaling in the microenvironment"
      ],
      "evidence_summary": "This program provides glioblastoma cells with a multifaceted survival advantage in hostile tumor microenvironments. Under hypoxic conditions, HIF-1α induction of LUCAT1 helps glioma stem-like cells maintain their self-renewal and tumorigenicity ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11300024/#:~:text=A%20new%20isoform%20of%20Lucat1,Depletion%20of%20LUCAT1%20impaired%20GSC)). At the same time, upregulation of SLC7A11 (xCT) supports an altered metabolic state with heightened glutathione-based antioxidant capacity, thereby reducing ROS accumulation and conferring resistance to chemotherapeutics like temozolomide ([pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27658422/#:~:text=resistance%20to%20oxidative%20stress%20and,and%20resistance%20to%20standard%20chemotherapy)). PGC-1α, a metabolic coactivator, is expressed in a subset of glioblastomas and has been linked to increased mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation; its suppression leads to ROS buildup and slower tumor growth, indicating that PGC-1α activity makes tumors more aggressive and therapy-resistant ([pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30578297/#:~:text=involved%20in%20tumor%20growth%20and,1%CE%B1%20displayed%20ROS)) ([pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30578297/#:~:text=PGC,glioblastoma%20therapies)). Moreover, this program subverts immune surveillance: NLRC5 downregulation is a known mechanism for glioblastoma to diminish MHC I antigen presentation, aiding in escape from cytotoxic T-cells ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4889388/#:~:text=Tumor%20antigen%20presentation%20to%20CD8,cell%20activation)). Additionally, high histamine signaling via H1 receptors in GBM has been associated with local immunosuppression (e.g., T cell dysfunction) and poorer patient outcomes ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11770814/#:~:text=Histamine%2C%20a%20key%20mediator%20of,open%20up%20a%20new%20avenue)). In summary, the genes in this program collectively allow GBM cells to thrive in low-oxygen, oxidative, and immunologically active conditions, promoting tumor persistence and progression despite therapy.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "reference": "Huang H. et al., Neuro Oncol, 2024",
          "id": "DOI:10.1093/neuonc/noae036",
          "type": "DOI",
          "notes": "Shows that LUCAT1 is induced by HIF-1α and NRF2 in hypoxic glioblastoma stem cells and that LUCAT1 supports hypoxia adaptation; knocking down LUCAT1 impaired GSC self-renewal and slowed tumor growth in vivo ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11300024/#:~:text=A%20new%20isoform%20of%20Lucat1,Depletion%20of%20LUCAT1%20impaired%20GSC)) ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11300024/#:~:text=gene%20expression%20and%20GSC%20adaptation,survival%20in%20GBM%20xenograft%20models))"
        },
        {
          "reference": "Polewski M.D. et al., Mol Cancer Res, 2016",
          "id": "DOI:10.1158/1541-7786.MCR-16-0028",
          "type": "DOI",
          "notes": "Demonstrates that increased SLC7A11 expression in GBM elevates glutathione levels and oxidative stress tolerance. SLC7A11 overexpression led to reduced ROS and enhanced resistance to oxidative damage and temozolomide, linking this transporter to therapy resistance in glioma ([pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27658422/#:~:text=resistance%20to%20oxidative%20stress%20and,and%20resistance%20to%20standard%20chemotherapy))"
        },
        {
          "reference": "Yoshihama S. et al., PNAS, 2016",
          "id": "DOI:10.1073/pnas.1602069113",
          "type": "DOI",
          "notes": "Identifies NLRC5 as a major target of cancer immune evasion. The study found that many tumors, including gliomas, exhibit genetic or epigenetic suppression of NLRC5, resulting in reduced MHC-I expression and impaired CD8+ T cell activation ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4889388/#:~:text=Tumor%20antigen%20presentation%20to%20CD8,cell%20activation))"
        },
        {
          "reference": "Bruns P. et al., Int J Cancer, 2019",
          "id": "PMID:30578297",
          "type": "PMID",
          "notes": "Reports that PGC-1α upregulation in glioblastoma enhances mitochondrial biogenesis and metabolic capacity. High PGC-1α expression was associated with worse survival, while its knockdown increased ROS and reduced proliferation and invasiveness of GBM cells, indicating PGC-1α drives a more aggressive, oxidative stress-resistant phenotype ([pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30578297/#:~:text=involved%20in%20tumor%20growth%20and,1%CE%B1%20displayed%20ROS)) ([pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30578297/#:~:text=PGC,glioblastoma%20therapies))"
        }
